  "stateOwnerDisposition": "MatrixDurableStore is the sole Matrix state writer and owns ingress projection, sync frontier, outbox, dispatch ledger, fenced claims, authority/content witnesses, entered-use proofs, append-only attempt history, legacy holds and durable recovery scheduling. No second sender or in-memory terminal ledger is admitted.",
  "terminalObserverDisposition": "Only authenticated Matrix sync reconciliation may qualify stable-transaction success or redaction. Transport acceptance is nonterminal; every entered or possibly entered fault remains an unknown external effect until durable reconciliation.",
  "transportTcbDisposition": "The only production physical-send composition is the statically linked safe-Rust MatrixSdkClient registered by TRANSPORT_TCB.json. Unsafe, FFI, dynamic-library and remote-sidecar physical-send modes are forbidden; target evidence must bind exact binary, configuration, process identity, runner and homeserver identities.",
  "clockDisposition": "Dispatch uses a durable monotonic epoch plus an independently observed wall-clock anchor. Large forward discontinuities fail the sender closed; rollback retains the monotonic anchor so grant lifetime cannot be extended. Protected target-host clock discipline remains external evidence.",
  "evidenceDisposition": "The ordinary-source observation is frozen at 712bc2e7e77bbb42b93d35ac4ea0730dabf572c5 / 87a2f91a1058322bc43bff690737c148fc9dc633. Read-only source-head and deterministic-merge lanes use one v2 command policy for locked all-target compilation, public API compile-fail proof, locked native plus repository regression tests with Q01-Q29 JUnit, strict Clippy, rustfmt, clean-tree, tracked-source provenance, paired acceptance and one readiness manifest. The external receipt binds the metadata candidate itself; real target, independent acceptance, activation and release remain separate.",
